Hearing this, you’re probably inclined to
think that all of the world’s code is stored

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.769
on AWS or maybe Azure given the title of the
video.

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:34.079
And you wouldn’t be wrong.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:38.899
Technically, it is stored on Azure but it’s
not because of Microsoft, it’s actually

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:44.760
thanks to one of their subsidiaries called
GitHub which they paid $7.5 billion for.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:51.850
GitHub is home to the code repos of Airbnb,
Shopify, Netflix, Robinhood, Reddit, DoorDash,

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:55.899
Walmart, and 90% of the Fortune 100.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:02.600
This translates to control over 100 million
developers, 4 million organizations, and 330

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.850
million repositories.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:08.020
Essentially, if you were able to hack into
GitHub’s servers, you would get access to

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:13.970
the entire world’s code whether it’s financials,
social media, games, ai, you name it.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:20.119
As GitHub likes to claim, “This is where
the world builds software” and now, it’s

00:01:20.119 --> 00:01:22.409
all controlled by Microsoft.

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:25.970
But how did one company end up getting so
much power over.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.060
Well, it wasn’t always like this.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.950
GitHub isn’t some sort of legacy tech company
founded in the 80s and 90s.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:39.560
GitHub was only founded 15 years ago in 2008
and it started off as just a regular old bootstrapped

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.280
startup funded by four ambitious engineers.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:50.360
Yet somehow, they’ve been able to convince
the entire world to jump on board, but is

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.549
this actually safe and responsible?

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:58.000
I mean, we’re essentially risking the entire
tech world and really much of the world economy

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
on Microsoft’s security measures.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.930
Well, join me as take a look back at how Microsoft
came to control the entire world’s code

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:09.979
and explore whether this is actually in the
world’s best interest or just Microsoft’s

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:16.010
best interest.

